amux — AI-native terminal control plane

usage: amux [command] [flags]

work:
  (bare)   open the dashboard (without a terminal, print this help)
  new      start a workgroup (no args: the create form)
  ls       workgroups and agents (state, PRs)
  open     open the dashboard on a workgroup or agent
  send     message an agent or workgroup (queued if busy; --now / --stop)
  add      add an agent to a workgroup
  archive  finish a workgroup (refuses while PRs are open)

manage:
  inbox    questions and follow-ups waiting for you
  repo     track the repositories agents get worktrees of
  device   phones and browsers that reach this machine directly (host only)
  cloud    reach this machine through Harness cloud
  harness  Claude Code / Codex installs and logins
  config   show or change amux settings (keybindings, Codex control, updates, ...)
  daemon   run or control the local daemon (restart loads a new binary)
  doctor   health check: versions, compatibility, dependencies and runtime
  update   install the latest amux release
  version  print CLI, daemon and database versions and compatibility
  help     help for amux or a command (help agent, help api, help --all)

more: rename · unarchive · rm · move · recreate · top · refresh · licenses
agents: amux help agent   scripting: amux help api

flags:
  -h, --help     show help for amux or for the command it follows
  -a, --all      with --help (and no command): print the entire help tree
  --all-help     print the entire help tree: every command, flag, action and example
  -v, --version  print CLI, daemon and database versions (same as amux version)

Set AMUX_SKIP=1 in your shell to bypass auto-launch.

Run 'amux <command> --help' for details. 'amux help --all' prints everything.
